      "text": "We need to solve the equation $7^{x+7} = 8^x$, where we aim at finding the expression for $x$ in the form $x=\\log_b 7^7$.\nTaking the $x$-th root on both sides and rearranging:\n$7=(\\frac87)^x$.\nSince $\\log_{\\frac87} 7 - x = -1$, and from $x=\\log_b 7^7$, we have $\\log_{\\frac87} 7 = \\log_b 7^7$.\nSo $\\frac1{-1}= \\log_b 7^7 = -7\\log_b  7 = -log_b 7^{-7}$.\nThis is equivalent to $-\\frac{1}{-1} = -7 \\implies \\boxed{7}$.\n*Note*: Idiot notation and I had $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{-1}=-7}$ :)\n$$7^{x+7} = 8^x => 7^{x+1} - 7^x = 0 =>\\frac{7^x}{1} - 7^x = 0=>(-1)(1)^x + 7^x = 0=>$$\n$\\boxed{x\\in\\{ 0\\}}$.Condiments :D",
